## Rebuttal
1. fixed — the capacity is the environment variable BISELLIUM_HEAVY_JOB_SLOTS, checked by readHeavyJobSlots as the first step of every takeHeavySlot and runInHeavySlot call, so the wrapper, runCi, runVerify and runBuilderCommand all refuse an out-of-domain value before a lease, a slot or a command (Input domain row 1; b1, b2, b3 and b4 rows). No file is read, so the gates job's record-reads preload (.github/workflows/ci.yml:72-77) sees nothing; the lazy read and its limit are gone.
2. fixed — no entry point reads a manifest for the capacity any more (heavyJobSlotsFor, the bisellium.yml key, the check.ts line and the Manifest field are removed), so "a reused lease reads no manifest" is now simply true; the brief says instead that the capacity check runs before lease reuse and that a reused lease prints nothing.
